# Analysis

## Focus Group Analysis — Automated Documentation using Amazon Q Developer (AWS)

---

# Overview

This section contains the complete analytical results produced during the focus group evaluation conducted as part of the Master's Degree research project on automated software documentation using Large Language Models (LLMs).

The analyses investigate the quality, usefulness, consistency, reliability, and practical adoption of AI-generated documentation produced through Amazon Q Developer (AWS) in a real industrial legacy system context.

The evaluation was performed through:

- automated JavaDoc generation;
- GitLab Merge Request review;
- qualitative focus group discussions;
- quantitative thematic analysis;
- integrated scientific interpretation.

---

# Research Objective

The primary objective of this study was to evaluate developers’ perceptions regarding automatically generated documentation in real software engineering environments.

The research focused on understanding:

- documentation quality;
- semantic value;
- contextual usefulness;
- consistency across classes;
- cognitive impact during code review;
- adoption feasibility in industrial workflows.

---

# Experimental Context

The experiment was conducted using:

- 10 real Java classes extracted from the SARSB legacy system;
- automated JavaDoc generation using Amazon Q Developer;
- a controlled GitLab Merge Request review process;
- a qualitative focus group involving experienced developers.

